<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Developer ID (non-App-Store) hardened-runtime entitlements for Cortex.

    This is the notarization-safe configuration for a Developer ID build that
    bundles a full CPython framework and native wheels. It is deliberately NOT
    the App Store sandbox model (see AppStore.entitlements / AppStoreChild.entitlements).
    App Sandbox is intentionally omitted because the Developer ID build writes
    cross-application MCP config and needs broad user file access, which the
    sandbox would break. That MAS-vs-DeveloperID trade-off is documented in
    docs/DISTRIBUTION.md and docs/APPLE_RELEASE.md.

    Every entitlement below exists because a bundled interpreter under the
    hardened runtime requires it to launch reliably and pass notarization.

    Quick Capture note: screenshot + highlight OCR capture runs ONLY in this
    Developer ID / DMG build (it is gated off in the MAS build via
    DistributionMode.isAppStore). It needs NO additional entitlements here:
      - Screen Recording and Accessibility are TCC runtime permissions, granted
        via the standard system prompts (NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription /
        AXIsProcessTrusted), not code-signing entitlements.
      - Global hotkeys / synthetic events via CGEvent + Carbon are not blocked
        by the hardened runtime and require no cs.* entitlement.
    So the cs.* keys below stay exactly as-is; nothing here impedes CGEvent or
    global hotkey registration.
  -->

  <!-- CPython's interpreter loop / regex / some C extensions map executable
       pages at runtime. Without JIT allowance the hardened runtime kills the
       interpreter on launch. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- The bundled interpreter and some native wheels allocate writable-then-
       executable memory. Required so the hardened runtime does not block that
       memory behavior. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- The app loads the bundled Python.framework and native .so wheels that we
       sign with our own Developer ID identity, not Apple's App Store child-cert
       model. Library validation would reject loading our own-signed dylibs from
       a different Team than the main executable's expectation, so it is disabled. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- The app sets PYTHON* environment variables (PYTHONHOME, PYTHONPATH, etc.)
       to point the bundled interpreter at the bundled stdlib and wheels. The
       hardened runtime strips DYLD_/PYTHON* style variables unless this is set. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Sign in with Apple (Guideline 4.8 — required alongside Google/GitHub sign-in). -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
  <array>
    <string>Default</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
